
====================================================================================================
(1) ring-average derivation of the scalar/photon ratio in B&O's model; physical cross-section ratio
====================================================================================================
  int (2+sin^2)^2 dx = 72/5, int (2-sin^2)^2 dx = 56/15;  ratio scalar/photon (2 photon pols) = 7/54
  x 3/(25 pi): 7/450/pi  (B&O: 7/(450 pi))
  ring average <(n.p)^2> = sin(theta)**2/2
  physical (incoherent) sigma_phiphi/sigma_gamgam at m = 0, by hand: 1/12
  module sigma_total(R,L) scalar/photon at s=1.0: 0.0833333333
  module sigma_total(R,L) scalar/photon at s=3.0: 0.0833333333

====================================================================================================
(2) eq. S11 massless limit and tau_phi/tau
====================================================================================================
  S11 at m = 0, N_phi = 0: dP/dt = 7/(450*pi) G^2 N^2 w^3 sigma^2   (B&O: 7/(450 pi))
  tau_phi/tau = (2 x 3/(25 pi))/(2 x 7/(450 pi)) = 54/7  (B&O: 54/7)

====================================================================================================
(3) resonant regime: S11 for w_s = m (1 + delta), delta -> 0; eq. 17 needs dP/dt -> G^2 N^2 sigma^2 N_phi m^3 delta/16
====================================================================================================
  delta = 0.01: [dP/dt]/(G^2 N^2 sigma^2 N_phi m^3 delta) = 0.0599282336472   (1/16 = 0.0625)
  delta = 0.0001: [dP/dt]/(G^2 N^2 sigma^2 N_phi m^3 delta) = 0.0624734461567   (1/16 = 0.0625)
  delta = 1.0e-6: [dP/dt]/(G^2 N^2 sigma^2 N_phi m^3 delta) = 0.0624997343759   (1/16 = 0.0625)
  with sigma = m v^2/2, delta = v^2/2: G^2 N^2 (m^2 v^4/4) N_phi m^3 (v^2/2)/16 = G^2 m^5 N^2 v^6 N_phi/128 (eq. 17)
  check S11 numerics at m = 1e-4, w = 1: J/(15360 pi) = 0.00495148678684;  7/(450 pi) = 0.00495148711841

